{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/evidence/C32/remediation-attempt-22/remediation.md docs/planning/evidence/C32/remediation-attempt-22/transition.json docs/planning/evidence/C32/remediation-attempt-22/source-boundary-final.log docs/planning/reviews/C31/attempt-07/verdict-returned.json'","aggregated_output":"# C32 attempt-22: Harness native presentation ownership\n\nActual attempt-22 returned 9/8/9/8/8, no blockers, with R1/E1 for a late Harness confirmation. Its raw verdict, transport, false full-gate audit and D034 acceptance remain unchanged. It accepted attempt-21's native omissions as remedied. This fix concerns C32 Harness tool decisions, not C31's closed configuration-review subject.\n\nThe real authority now allocates revocable presentation ownership when admitting a write-capable Harness approval. The effect carries that original lease into the existing production scoped confirmation API. Retiring or settling the pending decision drops/revokes its owner; retirement revokes before native dismissal. A delayed effect cannot create a fresh owner and register a stale sheet. Private settlement checks and command authority remain intact; no operation is replayed.\n\nTwo production-interface regressions use the real pinned engine, synthetic TLS Gateway, actual authority admission/delivery, and native adapter API. A fixture-only barrier pauses ConfirmHarness after admission releases its lock and before native registration. One test ends the conversation; the other retires its project binding. On the old unscoped production effect both fail with one native sheet registered versus zero expected. The first sandbox run could not bind loopback and is preserved separately, not called a reproduced race. The meaningful loopback old-red run failed both exact lifecycle assertions. Old production was the retained 358a524f tree plus the additive fixture barrier/tests, before the ownership fix. No contemporaneous full uncommitted-tree hash was captured for that old-red run; the raw command/log and reconstructable baseline/fixture seam are retained without inventing one.\n\nThe first green build hit a Rust borrow-check error and is retained. After narrowing the borrow, all eight affected Harness integration tests passed, including both race regressions, already-open late confirmation retirement, and fresh native Cancel/Allow controls. Formatting, fixture/default Clippy, generated bindings, five source/bundle-boundary validator tests, Python syntax and actual 20-driver/C44 cumulative mapping validation passed before sealing. The strict authority projection rejects changes outside the Harness state field, effect declaration, Harness approval arm, Harness effect arm and its fixture-only barrier match. No C31 production branch or C30/C31 assertion-map entry changed.\n\nG9's full application bundle, native records and original reviewed source are archived unchanged under `P09/native-history/Worf-generation-09-complete-before-C32-scoped-confirmation-20261102`. G10 is a new rebuild/qualification because production application bytes change. It requires all 20 current mapped drivers (the restored C32 driver is now included) and all 18 current repository checks once. It does not relabel G9 or the earlier supplemental audit as current G10 execution. Original controllers, transition variants, inventories, reviews and raw results stay preserved; new named production variants bind the new generation explicitly.\n\nC31 attempt-07 remains an actual audited full-nine review, without owner activation or a further C31 scoring/remediation cycle. Its original scope hashes are checked against unchanged files or exact archived reviewed inputs; the shared authority projection proves only C32 Harness ownership changed. New actual C32 and cumulative P09 reviews inspect that delta and administrative provenance. C30's owner all-nine decision and C41 standing remain separate; no C30 timing/scenario/remediation/re-review is performed. L19 remains fully charged with zero allowance, and no real credential, live product call, signing, installation or publication is authorized.\n\nQualification and new review results are not claimed here before execution. The Terminal-owned supervisor seals source and full bundle, allows one UI writer, preserves per-driver logs/results, fails on a real condition, and resumes only valid completed stages after ownership inspection. It proceeds to one actual fresh C32 attempt-23, then an actual P09 full-nine review; C31 is never sent for another review.\n{\n  \"schema\": \"airs-v2/c32-production-transition/1\",\n  \"prior_transition_sha256\": \"e0655b9f7276faba07416f0ae593ad1b012a9f7870ddf9fd322b31a8f541eb1d\",\n  \"source_delta\": {\n    \".gitattributes\": {\n      \"before\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"de958205ab9744bd4230440718420a24d0a8c8f5821603c91b416ebd7a1cc8ea\"\n      },\n      \"after\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"a11abe825e289e9b1ee6f55775791b9e2b607e68ce319839889f0d5cd0ef1052\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs\": {\n      \"before\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"6b3a6ef583acbd6aad4c40c3d0aef08c9f4336d540ccc58ef6855eb7b65de013\"\n      },\n      \"after\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"89fcb7cd19c21f7df62de25f4dde87e28cc5b7a6e89341a92b8ce007756812c2\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"crates/desktop-core/src/authority/harness_tools.rs\": {\n      \"before\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"11ad6583302ce043102179e7461828e78d84fe23e63ff44d5b80c7a099534483\"\n      },\n      \"after\": {\n        \"mode\": 420,\n        \"kind\": \"file\",\n        \"sha256\": \"c5185d1d1a6d11bc248551207683b8722d903e019dc50246a93924ca5e72a83b\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"crat